{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 50, :comments ["<b>And you, appoint the Levites over the Tabernacle of the Testimony.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): this explains what was said earlier, ״only the tribe of Levi you shall not number,״ and to say that the reason the Levites were not counted among the children of Israel was only for their preeminence — so that they would be the ministers of the Tabernacle." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״ואתה הפקד את הלוים״ — whoever draws himself near a little, they draw him near a lot. From where? From the children of Levi, who drew themselves near a little, as it is written (Exodus 32:26): ״מי לה׳ אלי ויאספו אליו כל בני לוי״ — 'Whoever is for HaShem, to me!' and all the children of Levi gathered to him. Therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, said: They drew near to Me, so I too draw them near and make them the ministers and great ones of My house, and I entrust My house only to them, as it is said: ״ואתה הפקד את הלוים על משכן העדות ועל כל כליו ועל כל אשר לו המה ישאו את המשכן ואת כל כליו והם ישרתוהו.״ It says ״over the Tabernacle of the Testimony״ — that is the Ark, in which is the testimony; ״and over all its vessels״ — they are the Menorah and the Table and the Altars; ״and over all that pertains to it״ — all the other utensils. ״They shall carry the Tabernacle״ — they are the bearers when the camps journey, and they are the ministers when they encamp."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:29:35.234728593Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}